# 4. Cheat Sheet Refresh

## Five Commands I Would Use First During an Incident

| Command                      | Why                                              |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `ps aux`                     | Check running processes and resource usage.      |
| `top`                        | Monitor CPU, memory, and processes in real time. |
| `systemctl status <service>` | Check service status.                            |
| `journalctl -u <service>`    | Review service logs.                             |
| `df -h`                      | Check filesystem disk usage.                     |

### My Basic Incident Flow

```text
Problem Reported
      ↓
Check Process
      ↓
Check Service
      ↓
Check Resources
      ↓
Check Logs
      ↓
Check Network / Port
      ↓
Take Corrective Action
      ↓
Verify
```

